# Live site is the target; local stays in parity

When the user talks about the site, pages, Dashboard, Resources, chrome, or “make this live,” they mean **production**:

- **Frontend:** Vercel project `kpf` → https://kpf-site.vercel.app (push `main`; root `frontend/`)
- **WordPress / CMS / plugin / theme / admin screens:** DreamHost → https://kpf.dreamhosters.com

Local (`frontend/` on :3010, wp-env on :8888) is a **copy of live**, not the place the user is looking.

## Required loop for any site change

1. **Edit locally** in this repo (`frontend/` and/or `wordpress/plugins/kpf-core`, `wordpress/themes/kpf-blank`). Never patch production without the same files on disk here.
2. **Ship live** in the same turn — do not stop at local:
   - Faust/Next UI: commit if asked, **push `main`** so Vercel deploys.
   - Plugin/theme/admin CSS/JS: **commit** the files that should go live, then `DH_SSH_KEY_FILE=…/.tmp/kpf-dreamhost-deploy scripts/deploy-dreamhost-wp.sh`. The script rsyncs **git HEAD**, not leftover dirty `kpf-core` files (Designs admin, `Preview.php`, maps). Rebuild webpack assets and commit `build/` before sync when SCSS/JS changed. Do not set `KPF_DEPLOY_FROM_WORKDIR` / `KPF_DEPLOY_ALLOW_DIRTY` to ship WIP.
3. **Done** only when live shows the change **and** the local tree matches what was deployed (same source + built CSS/JS). Hard-refresh / cache-bust if WP admin CSS looks stale.

Do not leave local-only diffs for UI the user will check on DreamHost or Vercel. Do not change live without writing it locally first.
